<%#
  Renders a single dropped (no-longer-orderable) cart line, with the diner's
  only way to unstick a cart around it — the wine went unavailable, its
  list was un-published, its price for this size fell to zero, or it was
  deleted outright. See Cart::DroppedItem for the shape and why #items
  alone can never recover from this on its own.

  Struck out and set on a different stock from the orderable lines above it,
  so the state reads before the sentence explaining it does: this is not a
  line of the bill, it is a line that has to go before there can be one.

  Locals:
    dropped    - the Cart::DroppedItem to render (required)
    restaurant - the owning Restaurant, for building the remove route (required)
%>
<% wine_name = dropped.wine&.name %>
<li class="panel wine-soldout">
  <%# No leader on this row: a leader runs a label to its value, and this
      line has no value left to run to — the tag is what replaced it. %>
  <p class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
    <span class="wine-name">
      <%= wine_name || t("cart.dropped_item.unknown_wine") %>
    </span>
    <span class="tag-out"><%= t("cart.dropped_item.unavailable") %></span>
  </p>

  <p class="note mt-2"><%= t("cart.dropped_item.reasons.#{dropped.reason}") %></p>

  <div class="mt-3 flex justify-end">
    <%# The accessible name must identify which line this removes — with
        two or more dropped lines sharing a size, and possibly no wine name
        at all once a wine is deleted, "Remove" alone would leave every
        control indistinguishable to a screen-reader user. Once wine is nil
        (the wine itself was deleted — the only branch that reaches the
        remove_unknown fallback) there is no bottle_size_ml left to report
        for a bottle line, so the bottle fallback drops the size entirely
        and names the serving instead; wine_id is still what tells two
        such lines apart. %>
    <%= button_to cart_items_path(restaurant_slug: restaurant.slug), method: :delete,
          params: { wine_id: dropped.wine_id, serving: dropped.serving, glass_size_ml: dropped.glass_size_ml },
          class: "btn-wine-outline shrink-0",
          "aria-label": wine_name ? t("cart.remove_item", wine: wine_name) :
            (dropped.serving == "bottle" ?
              t("cart.dropped_item.remove_unknown_bottle", wine_id: dropped.wine_id) :
              t("cart.dropped_item.remove_unknown", wine_id: dropped.wine_id, size: dropped.glass_size_ml)) do %>
      <%= icon "trash", class: "size-4" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</li>
